## STANDING DISCIPLINE

- No model logic changes during a validation window.
- No change without 50+ settled bets or a 4+ occurrence repeated pattern.
- **Net, not gross.** Every P&L number produced before 2026-09-01 is gross.
  ~3.6¢/contract. A band under ~+4 gross is dead until proven otherwise.
  **Estimate net BEFORE building, not after** — lows and treasuries both got
  built out before anyone did the arithmetic.
- **One fee observation is not a fee schedule.** Confirm 3.6¢ at a second price
  point before any real-money decision rests on it.
- Win rate ≠ profit. **Proof: `CONV/AGREE/70+` hits 75.4% and LOSES 2.09¢,
  because it pays 77.5¢ to do it.** Same for the 80+ band generally — 96.1% at
  94.4¢ pays +1.70.
- **Never pool strategy tags.** V530_, V531_, and FAV_V1_ are different models.
- **Never reconstruct a file from memory** — work from the current paste.
- **Check the sign convention before interpreting any bias number.**
- **Distinguish three populations:** the MARKET's top bracket, the MODEL's pick,
  and the manual research. Conflating them produces opposite conclusions.
- **Validation thresholds are counts, not dates.**
- **Write the kill line before the data arrives.** A threshold chosen after
  seeing forward results is not a threshold.
- **A cross-check is not optional.** The Denver 32°F row passed every quality
  flag its source provides.
- **Do not read ordering out of thin cells.** Twelve 15-minute cells of ~80
  correlated observations produced a scatter, and an earlier reading of it as a
  trend did not survive more data. Same trap caught the 71–72 cell, and the
  volume filter's n=20 decisive cell.
- **Underpowered ≠ disproven.** Volume was monotonic on 20 observations. That is
  neither a result nor a refutation — it is a re-test.
- **Always use ASK, never mid.** You pay the ask. Mid overstates every result by
  1–2 points. This caused two analyses of the same data to disagree on 55–59.
- **A band that comes out near zero may be two populations averaged together.**
  "55–59 doesn't work" was really 55–57 losing and 58–59 working. Before killing
  a band, split it.
- **Scheduled jobs start late, never early.** Any time-window check must be
  one-sided. A symmetric tolerance silently discards the whole late half.
- **Check every checkpoint on schedule.** The recurring failure is waiting out a
  full window, finding a defect at the end, and restarting the clock. Four times
  since May.
- Real-money config when go-live: $5 flat/bet, YES-only, conviction tier
  preferred, skip Phoenix (bracket-width problem), max 3–5 bets/day.

